# 232 · Teachers research the web with their program's own search and fetch

**Status:** `IN_PROGRESS` · **Version:** [v0.1.4](../roadmap.md#v014)

## What

The owner, issue 56 (2026-11-04): "Teachers are supposed to do independent research, but in the teacher logs I'm watching on v0.1.2 I'm seeing no web calls, no research happening." And on 2026-11-07: "claude code and codex provide their own web search and fetch tooling, those should be enabled for teachers... plain and simple..."

The teachers' instructions tell them to research outside the run (papers, upstream code, issues), but no tool let them. Codex ran with `web_search = "disabled"` and its standalone search off; Claude Code ran with `--tools ""`, none of its own tools; OpenCode denied `web`; and Thermite's archived fetch (`fetch_url`) reached Pi teachers alone, and only for the sites `fetch_domains` lists, none by default. On the lab, 2026-11-07, one teacher's 947 tool calls in a day read code, the knowledge base and the pages the workers had fetched: none reached the web.

1. **Claude Code teachers** get its WebSearch and WebFetch: `--tools "WebSearch,WebFetch"` and both in `--allowedTools`, headless and in their own terminal. No other tool of Claude Code's own.
2. **Codex teachers** get its web search: `web_search = "live"`, and `standalone_web_search` left on, headless and in their own terminal. Every other tool feature stays off.
3. **The teachers alone:** the auditor, the review panel, the merged by model, the synthesizer and the final writer keep none. Pi and OpenCode teachers are as before: Pi's `fetch_url` for the listed sites.
4. **Tests:** a teacher's Claude Code command line and a teacher's Codex configuration have the web tools; another advisor's do not.
5. **Every round** (the owner, 2026-11-08): a teacher with its program's web tools is told to search the web every round and to bring what it finds in by URL; in its own terminal, a turn that ends with no search or fetch in its call sends it back to search, twice at most, with a line on Live.
6. **A Codex teacher on Responses Lite:** for a model Codex drives over Responses Lite (its gpt-6 models, in Code Mode Only), Codex sends no hosted tools and offers its own search (`web.run`) only for a provider that says it has the search endpoint. The teacher's provider says so (`supports_standalone_web_search = true`), `web` is on the model's own list (`[features.code_mode]` `direct_only_tool_namespaces = ["web"]`, since Code Mode's host stays off), and the call's proxy lets a teacher's call, and no other, reach `POST /alpha/search` on a ChatGPT sign-in.
7. **Live shows a Codex search:** the rollout reader names a namespaced tool by both names (`web.run`) and reads the provider's own search (`web_search_call`) as a tool call.

## Why

The teachers bring a run its new opportunities. Without outside sources they rework what the run already holds; with them they can bring a paper's method, an upstream fix or a known issue to the queue.

## Done when

- [ ] Items 1 to 7.
- [ ] Pages: the advisors file (Claude Code and Codex for a teacher), Set up the advisors, How it fits together, Who holds your keys, the agents' roles, the changelog.
- [ ] On the lab, a teacher's round shows web searches or fetches on Live, and a citation of a URL in its portfolio.
- [ ] On the lab, in both campaigns, each teacher in Claude Code and in Codex searches the web in every round.

## Decisions

- 2026-11-08, the owner: "claude and codex should search every round. EVERY ROUND. you always go to bring external resources in when possible. same for the p100 campaign". Items 5 to 7 ([decisions](../decisions.md#research-and-judging)).
- 2026-11-07, the owner: "claude code and codex provide their own web search and fetch tooling, those should be enabled for teachers... plain and simple...". Thermite's own open fetch (`fetch_domains` `"*"`) still keeps the knowledge base away from that call; the programs' own web tools sit beside the knowledge base by this decision ([decisions](../decisions.md#research-and-judging)).

## Progress

- 2026-11-07 20:08 UTC: built. `web` on an advisor's tools (`supervisor/advisors/call.ts`), set for the teachers alone (`supervisor/advisors/pass/teachers.ts`). Claude Code: `--tools` and `--allowedTools` (`supervisor/advisors/runtimes/claude-code.ts`, `supervisor/advisors/tools/mcp.ts`, `supervisor/advisors/terminal/call.ts`). Codex: `web_search = "live"` and its standalone search not turned off (`agents/programs/codex/index.ts`, `supervisor/advisors/cli.ts`, `supervisor/advisors/terminal/profiles.ts`, `supervisor/advisors/runtimes/opencode-codex.ts`). Tests: `tests/supervisor/advisors/runtimes/cli.test.ts`, `tests/supervisor/advisors/terminal/profiles.test.ts`. The test files have not run yet: they run on the lab's VM.
- 2026-11-07 22:44 UTC: on the lab since the roll of 39e04adb (sparks-rig at 22:00 UTC), the teachers' round that restarted at 21:59 UTC: the teacher in Claude Code called `WebSearch` at 22:11:22 UTC ("DGX Spark GB10 cudaMalloc first touch page fault slow large allocation unified memory") among its 112 tool calls since 21:30 UTC; the teacher in Codex made no web search in its 8-minute round. Codex's search is not yet seen to be offered: the next rounds show it, or the request's tools at the model proxy.
- 2026-11-07 23:18 UTC: that round's portfolio, at 22:22 UTC, cites a page of NVIDIA's developer forums on slow mmap on the DGX Spark in one of its experiments: the Claude Code teacher's search reached the queue. The Codex teacher's search is still to be seen.
- 2026-11-08 08:29 UTC: in the 10 rounds from 21:58 UTC to 08:03 UTC, the Claude Code teacher made 2 web searches and 6 fetches, in 5 rounds of the 10 (NVIDIA's forums and CUDA guide, vLLM's code and an issue, an LTX-2 issue, the recipe's script); the Codex teacher made none in 11, and each of its rounds began with an `exec` call that Codex refused, `code-mode host is disabled`, six of them looking for a web tool. Why: Codex 0.162.1's model catalog marks gpt-6.1-sol `use_responses_lite` and `code_mode_only`. Codex then sends no hosted tools, `web_search = "live"` included, and offers its standalone search (`web.run`, which calls the provider's `alpha/search`) only for OpenAI's own provider or one marked `supports_standalone_web_search`; Thermite's provider was neither, so the teacher had no search at all, and in Code Mode Only it would reach `web.run` only from `exec`. Live would not have shown a Codex search either: the rollout reader read neither a namespaced tool's name nor `web_search_call`. OpenAI's page on ChatGPT plan usage lists only `POST /responses` and `GET /models`, and says web search depends on the model and the account; whether `alpha/search` answers a ChatGPT sign-in is seen on the lab. Built items 5 to 7. Tests: `tests/agents/model/chatgpt.test.ts`, `tests/agents/programs/codex/rollout.test.ts`, `tests/agents/cli/call.test.ts`, `tests/agents/roles/teacher.test.ts`, `tests/agents/roles/texts.test.ts`, `tests/supervisor/advisors/terminal/profiles.test.ts`; they run on the lab's VM.

